\section{Electric charges}

\subsection{Microscopic picture}
Matter is made of atoms. A proton carries charge $+e$, an electron $-e$,
with
\[
e = 1.60\times 10^{-19}\,\mathrm{C}.
\]
A neutral atom has equal numbers of protons and electrons.
\textbf{Charge is a property of particles}, not something ``painted on''.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.95]
  % atom
  \draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.35);
