\section{Conductors, insulators and charging}

\subsection{Conductors and insulators}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em]
  \item \textbf{Conductor:} many movable charge carriers
        (metals: free electrons; salt water: ions).
  \item \textbf{Insulator:} no freely movable carriers
        (plastic, nylon, glass, pure water, vacuum).
\end{itemize}
A metal sphere on a nylon thread can redistribute charge on its surface,
but charge cannot leak away through the thread.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
  % metal
  \draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.1);
  \foreach \x/\y in {-0.4/0.3,0.2/0.5,-0.2/-0.4,0.5/-0.2,0.0/0.0,0.4/0.15,-0.55/-0.1} {
    \fill[negC] (\x,\y) circle (1.6pt);
  }
