\section{Coulomb's law}

For two point charges in vacuum (or air),
\[
F = k\frac{|Qq|}{r^{2}},
\qquad
k = \frac{1}{4\pi\varepsilon_0} \approx 9.0\times 10^{9}\,\mathrm{N\,m^{2}\,C^{-2}}.
\]
$\varepsilon_0$ is the permittivity of free space.
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em]
  \item Direction: along the line joining the charges (repel / attract as above).
  \item More charge $\Rightarrow$ stronger force; further apart $\Rightarrow$ weaker ($1/r^{2}$).
  \item Scaling: if charges $\times n$ and separation $\times m$, then
        $F' = (n^{2}/m^{2})F$.
\end{itemize}

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \node[circle,draw,fill=gray!15,minimum size=8mm,font=\small] (A) at (0,0) {$Q$};
  \node[circle,draw,fill=gray!15,minimum size=8mm,font=\small] (B) at (4.2,0) {$q$};
  \draw[{Latex}-{Latex},thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,above] {$r$};
  \draw[-{Latex},thick,posC] ($(A)+(0.55,0.45)$) -- ++(1.0,0) node[above,font=\scriptsize] {$F$};
  \draw[-{Latex},thick,posC] ($(B)+(-0.55,0.45)$) -- ++(-1.0,0) node[above,font=\scriptsize] {$F$};
  \node[below,font=\small] at (2.1,-0.7) {Equal-and-opposite Coulomb forces};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

