\subsection{Resultant field --- superposition}
Fields add as vectors:
\[
\vec E = \vec E_1 + \vec E_2 + \cdots.
\]
On a line, use signed magnitudes. Off a line, resolve components
(same strategy as combining forces in Active Physics).

\subsection{Neutral point ($E = 0$)}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
Two charges & Where $E$ can vanish \\
\midrule
Same sign & Outside, nearer the \emph{smaller} $|Q|$ \\
Opposite signs & Outside, on the side of the \emph{smaller} $|Q|$ \\
 & (never between them --- both fields same way) \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
Set $k|Q_1|/r_1^{2} = k|Q_2|/r_2^{2}$ $\Rightarrow$
$r_1/r_2 = \sqrt{|Q_1|/|Q_2|}$.

