\section{Uniform electric field}

\subsection{Parallel plates}
A uniform field has constant $\vec E$ (straight, parallel, evenly spaced lines).
Between large parallel plates with p.d.\ $V$ and separation $d$:
\[
E = \frac{V}{d},
\]
directed from higher potential to lower (from $+$ plate towards $-$ plate).

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[very thick] (0,0) -- (0,2.6) node[above,font=\small] {$+$};
  \draw[very thick] (3.2,0) -- (3.2,2.6) node[above,font=\small] {$-$};
  \foreach \y in {0.4,0.9,1.4,1.9,2.4} {
    \draw[-{Latex},thick,gray!70] (0.25,\y) -- (2.95,\y);
  }
  \draw[{Latex}-{Latex}] (0,-0.35) -- (3.2,-0.35) node[midway,below,font=\scriptsize] {$d$};
  \node[font=\small] at (1.6,3.1) {$E = V/d$ (uniform)};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

