\ex
A battery is connected across a network of four identical resistors. What are the ammeter
readings $I_1$ to $I_4$?
\begin{center}
\begin{circuitikz}[scale=1.05, transform shape]
  % top battery
  \draw (0,3.4) to[battery1] (5.2,3.4);
  % left: 2A then R down
  \draw (0,3.4) to[ammeter, l=$2\,\mathrm{A}$] (0,2.2)
        to[R] (0,0.8)
        -- (0,0);
  % bottom: I1 then R then split
  \draw (0,0) to[ammeter, l_=$I_1$] (1.8,0)
        to[R] (3.4,0);
  % parallel pair
  \draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.7)
        to[ammeter, l=$I_2$] (4.4,0.7)
        to[R] (5.2,0.7)
        -- (5.2,0) -- (5.2,3.4);
  \draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,-0.7)
        to[ammeter, l_=$I_3$] (4.4,-0.7)
        to[R] (5.2,-0.7)
        -- (5.2,0);
  % right return ammeter
  \draw (5.2,0.7) to[ammeter, l=$I_4$] (5.2,2.4);
\end{circuitikz}
\end{center}
\sol[3.5cm]{%
The two series resistors and the return path carry the full battery current:
$I_1=2\,\mathrm{A}$, $I_4=2\,\mathrm{A}$.
The last two identical resistors are in parallel, so they share equally:
$I_2=I_3=1\,\mathrm{A}$.
}

