\noindent\textit{Example.}
Pump raises pressure $C\to A$ (cell raises potential).
First wheel: drop $P_A\to P_B$ (first bulb: drop $V_A\to V_B$).
Second wheel: further drop $B\to C$ (second bulb).
Same points match: pressure at $A,B,C$ $\leftrightarrow$ potential at $A,B,C$;
$V_{AC}=V_A-V_C$ $\leftrightarrow$ $P_A-P_C$.

\noindent\textit{Example.}
A cell of e.m.f.\ $1.5\,\mathrm{V}$ gives $1.5\,\mathrm{J}$ of electrical energy to every coulomb that
passes through it. If $4\,\mathrm{C}$ pass through the cell, energy supplied $=1.5\times 4=6\,\mathrm{J}$.


