\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.2em,itemsep=0.12em,topsep=0.25em]
  \item A \textbf{pump / cell} lifts the flow back up the hill (adds energy).
  \item A \textbf{wheel / bulb / resistor} is a slope down the hill (takes energy out of the flow).
  \item Ideal wire: flat path at constant height (same potential; no energy change).
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Two kinds of voltage: e.m.f.\ and p.d.}
The same unit (volt) is used in two places. Do not mix them up:

